  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a 44-year-old charity campaigner from Melton, Leicestershire, has died following an accident in Jordan. Paralysed from the chest down after a 2007 riding accident, she became known for raising nearly £1m for charity through endurance events. She completed the 2012 London Marathon in 17 days using a bionic suit, later lit the Paralympic cauldron in Trafalgar Square, and took part in the Great North Run while pregnant in 2016. Her family said they were devastated and asked for privacy."
